       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is five times the labeled maximum, and I don't know of any guideline supporting it. The risk is serious, with profound hypotension and prolonged shock, and amlodipine's long half-life means the effects would last for days. That's too much risk to enter on an unverified claim.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range**, up to 10 mg by mouth once daily. If standard dosing failed, the specialist may prefer adding another agent to raising amlodipine.\n- **Route the 50 mg order through pharmacy and the prescriber.** The specialist or attending can enter it directly with a documented rationale and a pharmacist's review. It should also include a monitoring plan, such as frequent blood pressure and heart rate checks.\n\nIf you want to go ahead with either of these, tell me. For the first, give me the dose you want, and I'll enter it now."
